  "equipment_type": "Heat pump",
  "applies_to": "Daikin Altherma low-temperature (LT) air-to-water heat pumps fitted with the DCOM-LT/MB (model number 534-001) P1P2-to-Modbus RTU interface, standard operating mode, per reference manual 534-252-A3.",
  "summary": "The DCOM-LT/MB is a small DIN-rail interface that sits on the Altherma P1P2 user-interface bus and exposes the heat pump as a Modbus RTU slave. Holding registers carry the commands and setpoints (on/off, mode, leaving water and room setpoints, domestic hot water, quiet mode, weather-curve offsets); input registers report the error state, running flags, temperatures and flow. Every register is one signed 16-bit word, with sensor temperatures in hundredths of a degree.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": null,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "0-based",
    "note": "The manual numbers registers by offset with 'Register Base 0', so the printed offset is the wire address. Its own example: holding register 1 = Modicon 40002, input register 20 = Modicon 30021."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "DCOM-LT/MB Reference Manual (English)",
    "doc_number": "534-252-A3",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.daikin.eu/content/dam/document-library/installation-manuals/ctrl/bms/dcom-lt-mb/DCOM-LT-MB_reference%20and%20installation%20manual_English.pdf",
    "pages": "p. 6 (protocol, function codes, special values, data types, holding registers), p. 7 (input registers), p. 8 (Modicon conversion, fault code decoding), p. 9 (sequencer mode)"
  },
  "notes": [
    "Three special values can come back from any register when read as 16-bit: 32767 = register unsupported, 32766 = not available in the current configuration, 32765 = value not loaded yet. Expect 32765 everywhere while the DCOM synchronises with the Altherma (up to 8 minutes after power-up).",
    "The manual types the setpoints and offsets as plain int16 with no scaling, so they are whole degrees; only the sensor temperatures (temp16) are in hundredths.",
    "The DCOM can also run in Sequencer mode (used with the DCOM-LT/IO variant) and Smart Grid mode, chosen with DIP switches SW1.1-SW1.2 (SW1.1-SW1.4 in Smart Grid mode). Sequencer mode moves several input registers (for example outside air to 133); those alternative registers are not listed here.",
    "Which functions actually work depends on the Altherma model and its user interface; unsupported ones return 32767 or 32766.",
    "The unit error code is two ASCII characters packed into one register: high byte = first character, low byte = second (for example 14152 = '7H'). The sub code is a separate number."
  ],
